      "body": "# Decisions extracted from the completed Rhino team worksheet\n\nThis is a transcription/normalization aid for the next repository agent. Do not treat ambiguous handwriting as stronger than the source PDF.\n\n## Compatibility\n- Automatic Feed Clamp: one physical clamp fits both SawMaster 18 and SawMaster 24; historical numbering differs for another reason. Both fit edges were marked approved.\n- Saw Vice Plate Set: two physically different sets, one per machine. Team marked that Rhino should sell them separately. The current single Shopify Product identity remains unresolved until a catalog split strategy is chosen.\n- All 38 non-blocked compatibility relationships in the prior worksheet were marked Approve.\n\n## Technical facts answered\n- BeadMaster 6: 110 V / 60 Hz; motor speed 3000 rpm.\n- ShapeMaster 6: 110 V / 60 Hz; motor speed 3000 rpm.\n- TrimMaster 8: 110 V / 60 Hz; motor speed 3000 rpm.\n- LapMaster 12: 110 V / 60 Hz.\n- LapMaster 18: 110 V / 60 Hz; motor power 1 hp.\n- SawMaster 18: 110 V / 60 Hz; 1.8 kW; 1700 rpm; 450 mm and 18 in marked as the same nominal blade size.\n- SawMaster 24: 110 V / 60 Hz; 1.8 kW; 1700 rpm; 600 mm and 24 in marked as the same nominal blade size.\n- Horsepower convention: manufacturer nameplate horsepower.\n- EM-1: 110 V; 1 hp; primary motor speed handwritten as <=5000 rpm (not an exact scalar); wheel operating range 0-3000 rpm; flexible-shaft range handwritten 500-5000 rpm; wheel diameter 6 in; wheel arbor 1 in; reservoir 3.5 gal; water system described as reservoir filtration with adjustable water outlets. Frequency and gallon convention were not definitively answered.\n\n## Measurement corrections answered\n- SawMaster 36 assembled first dimension corrected from 72 ft to 72 in.\n- LapMaster 18 net weight handwritten as 105 lb.\n- LapMaster 18 packed/shipping observation handwritten as 200 lb. Native Shopify shipping weight remains a separate domain.\n\n## EM-1 box contents\n- 80 grit selected instead of 60 grit.\n- 280 grit marked included.\n- Every listed contents row in the original checklist was marked Yes/included.\n- Moss filtration pads explicitly annotated quantity 2.\n- Exact quantities for most other lines were not explicitly written; do not infer them merely from inclusion.\n\n## File/resource decisions already answered\n- Canonical duplicate: LapMaster 12.pdf.\n- Canonical duplicate: LapMaster 18.pdf.\n- Canonical duplicate: BeadMaster.pdf.\n- Canonical duplicate: TrimMaster.pdf.\n- Videos 003 and 004 marked same content.\n- Videos 017 and 018 marked same content.\n- No first-priority resource publication-rights/language/current-version decisions were completed.\n\n## Abrasive grit\n- Grading standard written as CAMI.\n- Store manufacturer's printed grit number exactly.\n- For mixed-grit products/packs, store every included grit value.\n"
    },
